In short, you should interpret that lines in your example that only have numbers on their left but none on their right as reading right to left, otherwise the example becomes confusing.

This matrix is of grade 3. You can construct such matrices from the Grassman branch with
$$ \underbrace{\hat a}_{\,\text{ulant}} = 2 \overrightarrow{a}
 \qquad &
 \overrightarrow{a} = 3 \{a,b,c\} \\
\underbrace{a}_{\,\text{mnut}} = 2 \overleftrightarrow{a}
 \qquad &
 \overleftrightarrow{a} = 3 \{ \, a,b,c \, \} \\
$$
where the graded generators are represented by a Gell-Mann 3x3 matrix. For example the first line in your example matrix would then be
$$ Y_{31} = \overrightarrow{a_3} \otimes I_3 $$
The resulting matrix is the SU(3) starting element in an antisymetric representation. Also $\sigma^\pm$ give rise to 3x3-grads in the tensor product.
The answer is now simply
$$ Y \sim 3 \times 8^{\underset{\scriptstyle{\tiny \text{sym}}}+} (q_2) \times 8^{\underset{\scriptstyle{\tiny \text{sym}}}+} (q_3)$$

